{
  "decision": "CONFIRMED_SOURCE_CONFIGURATION_DELEGATES_LIMIT_AND_PUBLISHES_8GI_JUDGE_DEFAULT_FOR_MOLECULAR",
  "task_id": "molecular_self_assembly",
  "reviewer": "/root/astra_reporting_requirement_coverage; same prior independent source/native-result reviewer, source complement only",
  "question": "Does the acquired pinned task/harness itself establish an external 1GB cap that would explain the original helper not enforcing the README memory promise?",
  "conclusion": "No 1GB external cap is established by the pinned task/harness configuration examined. The task JSON omits memory limits. The acquired official leaderboard Kubernetes experiment files explicitly list Molecular with no override and a shared judge limit of 8g, translated by the original backend to an 8Gi container limit. That aggregate bound is not a per-solution 1GB check. This resolves the source-configuration question, while actual deployed overrides/admission policies remain unknown.",
  "source_revision": "6e4e5f4aa087a9121aa09a6059e5484e5102c6ff",
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact": "The exact task manifest has no work.mem_limit or judge.mem_limit. The original parser gets these absent values as None.",
      "refs": [
        "tasks/molecular_self_assembly.json (whole 2192-byte file)",
        "sforge/harness/task_spec.py:217-218,231-232"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "SForgeConfig defaults both work/judge memory limits to None. CLI and experiment values can supply resource policy. Per-task experiment values override experiment defaults; CLI-selected values take precedence when already present.",
      "refs": [
        "sforge/harness/config.py:67-70,194-201",
        "sforge/harness/experiment.py:207-216,257-271",
        "sforge/cli.py:443-449,1020-1025,1036-1039"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "All four acquired all-tasks-k8s experiment YAMLs describe themselves as official leaderboard settings and list Molecular with an empty override. Their inherited judge memory is 8g; work memory is 16g. This is a concrete published configuration, not evidence of an actual deployed run.",
      "refs": [
        "examples/all-tasks-k8s/experiment.yaml:1-4,41-51,96",
        "examples/all-tasks-k8s/experiment-codex.yaml:40-42,87",
        "examples/all-tasks-k8s/experiment-deepseek.yaml:45-47,101",
        "examples/all-tasks-k8s/experiment-glm.yaml:45-47,104"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "The configured judge limit is forwarded from run registration into judge submission and resolved as config over task. K8s applies it to the container requests and limits; 8g becomes 8Gi. There is no conversion into a per-case child limit in this path.",
      "refs": [
        "sforge/harness/run_agent.py:392-393",
        "sforge/harness/judge_server.py:505-524",
        "sforge/harness/run_evaluation.py:163-172",
        "sforge/harness/backend/k8s_backend.py:213-224,243-244,747-756"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fact": "Other supported backends do not imply a hidden 1GB default: Docker forwards mem_limit only when non-None; E2B warns that per-container CPU/memory values are ignored and uses template-level resources. Docker host policy and E2B template resources cannot be recovered from these defaults alone.",
      "refs": [
        "sforge/harness/backend/docker_backend.py:121-125",
        "sforge/harness/backend/e2b_backend.py:265-273"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "scientific_effect": {
    "closed": "The available exact source does not provide the hypothesized external 1GB enforcement. Its published official K8s setting instead provides an aggregate 8Gi judge cap.",
    "preserved_native_fact": "The unchanged original run_case accepted a child with measured RSS 1220866048 bytes and valid output on the official case under our explicit 2GiB regime. The lower-memory positive control also passed.",
    "not_established": "Whether any historical leaderboard deployment added a stricter 1GB per-child cap, changed CLI settings, admission policy, wrapper, or runtime limit; incidence and full-pool scoring impact.",
    "scope": "Source-level missing per-solution enforcement remains supported; benchmark-wide deployed-policy violation is not promoted. Container-level 8Gi shared by the parallel evaluator is not eight independent per-child 1Gi allocations or guarantees.",
    "disposition": "No task exclusion, certification, repair or new native execution in this complement. Root may adjudicate the finite contract finding separately."
  },
  "remaining_specific_decisive_fact": "For a historical hosted-policy claim, obtain the exact effective judge pod/container resource and per-child enforcement policy for that run; neither generic defaults nor comments claiming official settings prove deployment.",
